# DevSync conventions

This repo is a team project. Every feature must follow the same architecture and UI patterns. Do not invent a second style.

## Clean architecture

### Layers

```text
Presentation (screens, widgets, Cubit) → Domain (entities, use cases, contracts) → Data (impl, models, sources) → Firebase
```

Domain must not import Flutter UI, Cubit, GetIt, Firebase, or Data.

### Feature layout

Canonical tree for every feature:

```text
lib/features/<feature>/
  presentation/
    screens/     # route-level *Screen widgets (*_screen.dart)
    widgets/
    cubit/       # when the feature has app state
  domain/        # when talking to Firestore/API
  data/
```

- Folder name is **`screens`**, file/class is `*_screen.dart` / `*Screen`. Never use `pages/` with `*_screen.dart`.
- Auth is the Firestore template: domain → data → presentation with Cubit + `Result`/`Failure` + GetIt in `lib/core/di/injection.dart`.
- Skip Domain/Data for tiny local-only UI; still keep screens under `presentation/screens/`.
- Feature DI helpers are OK if invoked from `configureDependencies()` (one composition root).

### Convergence (do when touching that feature)

- **Projects** — move `screens/` and `widgets/` under `projects/presentation/`; add domain + `Result` repos when Firestore-backed.
- **Matching** — migrate `MatchingController` → Cubit(s) registered via `injection.dart`.
- **Profile / requests** — when leaving dummy data, copy auth’s domain/data/Cubit pattern.
- **Shell** — optional `shell/presentation/screens/` (navigation host only; low priority).
- Disambiguate duplicate names across features (e.g. two `ProjectDetailsScreen`s).

### Shared vs feature-owned

Promote to `lib/core/` when **another feature will use it**. Do not hide shared contracts inside auth.

| Shared in `core/` | Stays in the feature |
|---|---|
| `Result<T>`, `Failure` and the standard failure types | Firebase / API mapping (`mapAuthError`) |
| GetIt composition root, `UseCase`, `FirestoreCollections` | Entities, use cases, Cubits, screens |
| `Ds*` widgets, theme, icons | Feature widgets (`AuthScaffold`) |

### Errors (normalized)

All repositories return `Result<T>` from `lib/core/result/result.dart`.

Map errors at the repository boundary to types in `lib/core/error/failures.dart`:

- `NetworkFailure`
- `NotFoundFailure`
- `PermissionFailure`
- `ValidationFailure`
- `AuthFailure` (session / credentials — any feature)
- `CancelledFailure` (user dismissed Google/GitHub)
- `UnexpectedFailure` (never pass raw exception text to the UI)

Add a **feature-only** `Failure` subclass (example: `EmailNotVerifiedFailure`) only when no other feature will need that type.

Do not add dartz. Do not throw `FirebaseAuthException` into Cubits or widgets.

### State

Cubit first (`flutter_bloc`). GetIt for DI. Screens render states; they do not call Firebase.

Copy `lib/features/auth/` when a feature talks to Firestore. Skip Domain/Data for tiny local-only UI.

## Typography / page headers

Headings and type roles are **app-wide**. Do not invent feature-local heading widgets.

### Source of truth

- Fonts, weights, sizes → `Theme.of(context).textTheme` from `lib/core/theme/app_typography.dart`
- Page intro composition → `DsPageHeader` in `lib/core/widgets/ds_page_header.dart`
- Shared widgets live in `lib/core/`; do not add `features/*/widgets/*_heading.dart` for the same pattern

### Page headers

| Need | Use |
|---|---|
| Auth / marketing intro (teal uppercase eyebrow) | `DsPageHeader` default / `DsPageHeaderStyle.brand` |
| List / feature page title (muted meta like `2 listed` + large title) | `DsPageHeader(style: DsPageHeaderStyle.page, …)` |
| Top chrome (menu, back, actions) | `DsAppBar` only — compact title |

- `displaySmall` is the canonical in-body page title (~30 / w800). Prefer the theme role over ad-hoc `copyWith(fontSize: …)` for page titles.
- When the body already has `DsPageHeader` (`page`), do not duplicate that large title in `DsAppBar`.

### Anti-patterns

- One-off `ProjectsPageHeading` / `*PageHeading` per feature
- Hardcoding heading font sizes/weights that already exist as `TextTheme` roles
- Using `DsAppBar` as the primary large page title on list screens
